# Project Workflows

## Content Management Workflow

### Adding New Portfolio Items
1. Open `constants/data/portfolio.ts`
2. Add new portfolio object to the array:
   ```typescript
   {
     id: "portfolio-x",
     title: "Project Name",
     category: "Project Category", 
     tags: "tag1, tag2, tag3",
     img: "/assets/work-images/project-image.jpg",
     link: "#portfolioX",
     modal: {
       title: "Project Name",
       project: "Project Type",
       client: "Client Name",
       languages: "Tech Stack",
       preview: "preview-url.com",
       link: "https://live-site.com",
       description: "Detailed project description...",
       img: "/assets/work-images/project-detail.jpg"
     }
   }
   ```
3. Add project images to `public/assets/work-images/`
4. Test the portfolio page to ensure proper display

### Updating Personal Information
1. Edit `constants/data/personalInfo.ts`
2. Update any field in the `personalInfo` object:
   - `information.name` - Your name
   - `information.profession` - Job title/description
   - `information.experience` - Years of experience
   - `information.email` - Contact email
   - `information.location` - Current location
   - `information.socialMedia` - Social media links
   - `body` - About me paragraph

### Managing Navigation Menu
1. Open `constants/data/menu.ts`
2. Modify `menuItems` array:
   - Set `enabled: false` to hide menu items
   - Set `enabled: true` to show menu items
   - Update `name`, `link`, or `icon` as needed
3. Available FontAwesome icons are defined in `components/icon/Icon.fontawesome.ts`

### Adding New Skills/Services
1. Edit `constants/data/skills.ts`
2. Add new skill object:
   ```typescript
   {
     id: "skill-x",
     skill: "Service Name",
     about: "Description of the service...",
     img: "/assets/icons/service-icon.svg",
     bgColor: "bg-custom-color"
   }
   ```
3. Add service icon to `public/assets/icons/`

### Updating Experience/Education
1. **Experience**: Edit `constants/data/experience.ts`
2. **Education**: Edit `constants/data/education.ts`
3. Add new entries with:
   - `year` - Time period
   - `title` - Position/Degree title
   - `subTitle` - Company/Institution
   - `bgColor` - Background color class

## Development Workflow

### Local Development Setup
1. Clone repository
2. Install dependencies: `npm install`
3. Copy environment variables: `cp env.example.txt .env.local`
4. Configure Google OAuth credentials
5. Start development server: `npm run dev`

### Making Content Changes
1. Identify the correct constant file in `constants/data/`
2. Make changes directly to the TypeScript constants
3. TypeScript will validate changes automatically
4. Save file and see changes in browser (hot reload)
5. Commit changes to version control

### Testing Changes
1. **Type Check**: `npm run check-types`
2. **Lint**: `turbo lint`
3. **Build Test**: `npm run build`
4. **Manual Testing**: Check affected pages/components

### Deployment Workflow
1. Test all changes locally
2. Run full build: `npm run build`
3. Commit and push to main branch
4. Deploy to hosting platform (Vercel/Netlify)

## Asset Management

### Images
- **Portfolio Images**: `public/assets/work-images/`
- **Service Icons**: `public/assets/icons/`
- **Profile Photos**: `public/assets/about/`
- **Blog Images**: `public/assets/blog-images/`

### Adding New Images
1. Optimize images (WebP format preferred)
2. Add to appropriate asset directory
3. Reference in constants with path like `/assets/folder/image.webp`
4. Update alt text and descriptions as needed

## Content Strategy

### Portfolio Projects
- **Show Best Work**: Highlight 4-6 strongest projects
- **Diverse Categories**: Include different types of work
- **Complete Information**: Ensure all modal fields are filled
- **Working Links**: Verify preview and live site links

### Skills/Services  
- **Core Competencies**: Focus on primary services offered
- **Clear Descriptions**: Explain what each service includes
- **Visual Consistency**: Use consistent icon style and colors

### Personal Branding
- **Professional Bio**: Keep bio concise but informative
- **Current Information**: Regularly update experience and contact info
- **Social Links**: Ensure all social media links are current and active
